{"activity_text": "Antifungal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (97.87%) to MtDef4_V5 C: 17%, R: 19%. The A15L change made V6 more hydrophobic. Activity: active against B. cinerea (MIC 6 uM). Recombinant production:yeast:Pichia pastoris: activity tested using recombinant peptide. Antimicrobial robustness: KCl-insensitive:B. cinerea (100 mM), CaCl2-insensitive:B. cinerea (2 mM). The creation of a cationic surface via mutations made the peptide more competitive than cation in bacterial targeting. Plant protection:N. benthamiana: MtDef4_V6 was more potent in reducing lesions formed by the grey mould disease than either MtDef4 or MtDef4_V5.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "38619888", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Mol Plant Pathol. 2024 Apr;25(4):e13458. doi: 10.1111/mpp.13458. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04240", "source_id": "AP04240", "source_numeric_id": "04240", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04240", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Modes of action and potential as a peptide-based biofungicide of a plant defensin MtDef4", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
